4:02:59 PM [express] GET /api/lessons 304 in 17ms :: [{"id":"c3151c6b-b3ba-43a3-b066-b0535adb5415","title":"The Arabic Letter System","titleAr":"نظام الحروف العربية","description":"Discover how Arabic letters change shape based on their position in a word. Learn the 4 forms: isolated, initial, medial, and final — starting with Alif (أ), Ba (ب), Ta (ت), and Tha (ث).","descriptionAr":"اكتشف كيف تتغير أشكال الحروف العربية حسب موقعها في الكلمة. تعلّم الأشكال الأربعة: المنفرد، البداية، الوسط، والنهاية","level":1,"orderIndex":1,"category":"alphabet","skillFocus":"reading","imageUrl":null,"xpReward":60,"isPublished":true,"actflLevel":"Novice Low","cefrLevel":"A1","objectives":["Recognize all 28 Arabic letters in their isolated forms","Identify letter families by shared base shapes","Distinguish letters by their dot patterns","Write basic letter shapes with correct stroke direction","Pronounce each letter with its correct sound"],"canDoStatements":["I can recognize Arabic letters when I see them","I can name the 28 letters of the Arabic alphabet","I can write individual Arabic letters","I can pronounce each letter's basic sound"],"prerequisites":[],"estimatedMinutes":25},{"id":"fcc364c5-9911-4ee8-8a5d-5a4f8eb3a520","title":"Reading with Tashkeel: Arabic Vowel Marks","titleAr":"القراءة بالتشكيل: الحركات العربية","description":"Master the 8 essential diacritical marks that make Arabic readable. Learn Fatha (ـَ), Damma (ـُ), Kasra (ـِ), Sukun (ـْ), Shadda (ـّ), Tanween (ـًـٌـٍ), and long vowels. Without tashkeel, Arabic text is ambiguous — with it, every word has one clear pronunciation.","descriptionAr":"أتقن علامات التشكيل الثمانية الأساسية التي تجعل العربية قابلة للقراءة. تعلّم الفتحة والضمة والكسرة والسكون والشدة والتنوين والحروف المدّية","level":1,"orderIndex":2,"category":"alphabet","skillFocus":"reading","imageUrl":null,"xpReward":70,"isPublished":true,"actflLevel":"Novice Low","cefrLevel":"A1","objectives":["Read Arabic letters with all vowel marks (Fatha, Damma, Kasra, Sukun, Shadda)","Understand how tashkeel determines pronunciation","Distinguish between short and long vowels","Read fully vowelized Arabic words"],"canDoStatements":["I can read any Arabic word that has full tashkeel marks","I can identify the 3 short vowels and their sounds","I can explain what Sukun and Shadda do to a letter","I can distinguish long vowels from short vowels"],"prerequisites":["c3151c6b-b3ba-43a3-b066-b0535adb5415"],"estimatedMinutes":30},{"id":"d6f23458-f5c9-47fe-adce-7e309aec5ba4","title":"Connecting Letters: Your First Words","titleAr":"وصل الحروف: كلماتك الأولى","description":"Arabic is written in connected script. Learn how Ba, Ta, and Tha connect to form real words like بَاب (door), بِنْت (girl), and تَمْر (dates). Understand the dot system that distinguishes similar letters.","descriptionAr":"العربية تُكتب متصلة. تعلّم كيف تتصل الباء والتاء والثاء لتكوين كلمات حقيقية مثل باب وبنت وتمر","level":1,"orderIndex":3,"category":"alphabet","skillFocus":"reading","imageUrl":null,"xpReward":60,"isPublished":true,"actflLevel":"Novice Low","cefrLevel":"A1","objectives":["Connect Arabic letters to form real words","Understand how letter forms change by position","Read simple Arabic words in connected script","Write connected Arabic words"],"canDoStatements":["I can read simple connected Arabic words like باب and بنت","I can write Arabic words in connected script","I can identify which letters connect and which do not"],"prerequisites":["fcc364c5-9911-4ee8-8a5d-5a4f8eb3a520"],"estimatedMinutes":25},{"id":"ddeeec6b-63bf-46cf-bc0a-15b266d084b1","title":"The Sun & Moon Letters","titleAr":"الحروف الشمسية والقمرية","description":"Why do Arabs say 'ash-shams' but 'al-qamar'? Learn the 14 Sun Letters and 14 Moon Letters — the key to correct Arabic pronunciation and the definite article 'al' (الـ).","descriptionAr":"لماذا نقول الشَّمس ولكن القَمَر؟ تعلّم الحروف الشمسية والقمرية وتأثيرها على لام التعريف","level":1,"orderIndex":4,"category":"alphabet","skillFocus":"speaking","imageUrl":null,"xpReward":70,"isPublished":true,"actflLevel":"Novice Mid","cefrLevel":"A1","objectives":["Classify all 28 letters as Sun or Moon letters","Correctly pronounce the definite article ال with both types","Understand assimilation rules for Sun letters","Apply Sun/Moon rules when reading aloud"],"canDoStatements":["I can say الشَّمس and القَمَر with correct pronunciation","I can predict how ال sounds before any letter","I can read words with the definite article correctly"],"prerequisites":["d6f23458-f5c9-47fe-adce-7e309aec5ba4"],"estimatedMinutes":25},{"id":"d9a0d0af-1c1a-4552-b0a0-91d4bcd2bd20","title":"Essential Greetings & Responses","titleAr":"التحيات والردود الأساسية","description":"Master the art of Arabic greetings. Each greeting has a specific response: السلام عليكم → وعليكم السلام. Learn 8 greeting pairs used daily across the Arab world, with cultural context.","descriptionAr":"أتقن فن التحيات العربية. كل تحية لها رد محدد. تعلّم ٨ أزواج من التحيات المستخدمة يومياً","level":1,"orderIndex":5,"category":"conversation","skillFocus":"speaking","imageUrl":null,"xpReward":70,"isPublished":true,"actflLevel":"Novice Mid","cefrLevel":"A1","objectives":["Use 8 essential Arabic greeting pairs correctly","Respond appropriately to each greeting","Understand the cultural context of Arabic greetings","Greet people in formal and informal settings"],"canDoStatements":["I can greet someone in Arabic and respond to their greeting","I can say hello, goodbye, and thank you in Arabic","I can use the right greeting for the time of day"],"prerequisites":["d6f23458-f5c9-47fe-adce-7e309aec5ba4"],"estimatedMinutes":20},{"id":"5415ac5a-f22c-45e2-853d-f0ae58fbcc65","title":"Numbers & the Arabic Counting System","titleAr":"الأرقام ونظام العد العربي","description":"Arabic numbers look different from Western digits! Learn ٠١٢٣٤٥٦٧٨٩, count from واحد to عشرة, and discover that Arabic numbers are read left-to-right even though text goes right-to-left.","descriptionAr":"الأرقام العربية تختلف عن الأرقام الغربية! تعلّم العد من واحد إلى عشرة واكتشف أن الأرقام تُقرأ من اليسار لليمين","level":1,"orderIndex":6,"category":"vocabulary","skillFocus":"reading","imageUrl":null,"xpReward":60,"isPublished":true,"actflLevel":"Novice Mid","cefrLevel":"A1","objectives":["Read and write Arabic numerals ٠-٩","Count from 1 to 10 in Arabic","Understand the left-to-right number reading direction","Use numbers in basic contexts (prices, phone numbers)"],"canDoStatements":["I can count from 1 to 10 in Arabic","I can read Arabic numerals on signs and prices","I can write numbers using Arabic script"],"prerequisites":["d6f23458-f5c9-47fe-adce-7e309aec5ba4"],"estimatedMinutes":25},{"id":"f5322431-e8f8-42a6-ba7a-0d2db713a08f","title":"Arabic Root System: The Key to Vocabulary","titleAr":"نظام الجذور: مفتاح المفردات","description":"Arabic words are built from 3-letter roots. The root ك-ت-ب (k-t-b) gives us: كِتاب (book), كاتِب (writer), مَكتَبة (library), كَتَبَ (he wrote). Master this pattern to unlock thousands of words.","descriptionAr":"الكلمات العربية مبنية من جذور ثلاثية. الجذر ك-ت-ب يعطينا: كتاب، كاتب، مكتبة، كتب. أتقن هذا النمط لتفتح آلاف الكلمات","level":2,"orderIndex":1,"category":"vocabulary","skillFocus":"reading","imageUrl":null,"xpReward":80,"isPublished":true,"actflLevel":"Novice High","cefrLevel":"A2","objectives":["Identify 3-letter roots in Arabic words","Derive related words from a single root","Recognize common root patterns (Form I-X)","Use root knowledge to guess word meanings"],"canDoStatements":["I can find the root letters in common Arabic words","I can recognize word families built from the same root","I can guess the meaning of new words using root knowledge"],"prerequisites":["ddeeec6b-63bf-46cf-bc0a-15b266d084b1","5415ac5a-f22c-45e2-853d-f0ae58fbcc65"],"estimatedMinutes":35},{"id":"ffc98636-1efa-4029-bc8e-5473f63dd26c","title":"The Arabic Sentence: No 'Is' Needed","titleAr":"الجملة الاسمية: لا حاجة لـ is","description":"Arabic doesn't use 'is/am/are' in present tense! 'أنا طالب' literally means 'I student' = I am a student. Learn how Arabic nominal sentences work and build your first 10 sentences.","descriptionAr":"العربية لا تستخدم فعل الكون في المضارع! 'أنا طالب' تعني I am a student. تعلّم الجملة الاسمية","level":2,"orderIndex":2,"category":"grammar","skillFocus":"writing","imageUrl":null,"xpReward":80,"isPublished":true,"actflLevel":"Novice High","cefrLevel":"A2","objectives":["Build nominal sentences without a verb (الجملة الاسمية)","Use personal pronouns with nouns and adjectives","Express identity and descriptions in present tense","Understand word order in Arabic sentences"],"canDoStatements":["I can introduce myself using أنا + noun","I can describe people and things without using a verb","I can build 10+ simple Arabic sentences"],"prerequisites":["f5322431-e8f8-42a6-ba7a-0d2db713a08f"],"estimatedMinutes":30},{"id":"67172fb0-4c96-4d90-9abe-0360de06dea3","title":"Masculine & Feminine: The Ta Marbuta","titleAr":"المذكر والمؤنث: التاء المربوطة","description":"Most Arabic feminine words end with ة (ta marbuta). مُعَلِّم (male teacher) → مُعَلِّمة (female teacher). Learn this pattern to double your vocabulary instantly and speak correctly about people and objects.","descriptionAr":"معظم الكلمات المؤنثة تنتهي بـ ة. معلِّم → معلِّمة. تعلّم هذا النمط لمضاعفة مفرداتك فوراً","level":2,"orderIndex":3,"category":"grammar","skillFocus":"writing","imageUrl":null,"xpReward":80,"isPublished":true,"actflLevel":"Intermediate Low","cefrLevel":"A2","objectives":["Transform masculine words to feminine using ة","Apply gender agreement in sentences","Identify natural vs. grammatical gender","Use gender correctly with professions and nationalities"],"canDoStatements":["I can make any profession feminine by adding ة","I can use the correct gender when describing people","I can double my vocabulary using the masculine/feminine pattern"],"prerequisites":["ffc98636-1efa-4029-bc8e-5473f63dd26c"],"estimatedMinutes":25},{"id":"73a879d7-59c0-48d7-9006-9f46b7d4c3ba","title":"At the Souk: Shopping Dialogue","titleAr":"في السوق: حوار التسوّق","description":"Navigate a real Arabic marketplace! Practice a full shopping dialogue: asking prices (بِكَم هذا؟), bargaining (غالي! — Too expensive!), and completing a purchase. Cultural tip: bargaining is expected and enjoyed.","descriptionAr":"تجوّل في سوق عربي حقيقي! تدرّب على حوار كامل: السؤال عن الأسعار، المفاوضة، وإتمام الشراء","level":2,"orderIndex":4,"category":"conversation","skillFocus":"listening","imageUrl":null,"xpReward":80,"isPublished":true,"actflLevel":"Intermediate Low","cefrLevel":"A2","objectives":["Navigate a shopping dialogue in Arabic","Ask prices and negotiate politely","Use demonstrative pronouns (this/that)","Complete a purchase transaction in Arabic"],"canDoStatements":["I can ask how much something costs in Arabic","I can negotiate a price at a market","I can complete a basic shopping interaction"],"prerequisites":["67172fb0-4c96-4d90-9abe-0360de06dea3","d9a0d0af-1c1a-4552-b0a0-91d4bcd2bd20"],"estimatedMinutes":30},{"id":"7014428a-55c4-4b90-9406-7b4433885789","title":"Food Culture & Restaurant Arabic","titleAr":"ثقافة الطعام وعربية المطاعم","description":"Order food like a local! Learn menu vocabulary, how to order (أريد... من فضلك), express preferences (بدون ملح — without salt), and understand common dishes: حُمُّص، فَلافِل، شاوَرما، كُنافة.","descriptionAr":"اطلب الطعام كالسكان المحليين! تعلّم مفردات القائمة وكيف تطلب الطعام وتعبّر عن تفضيلاتك","level":2,"orderIndex":5,"category":"conversation","skillFocus":"speaking","imageUrl":null,"xpReward":75,"isPublished":true,"actflLevel":"Intermediate Low","cefrLevel":"A2","objectives":["Order food at an Arabic restaurant","Express food preferences and restrictions","Read a basic Arabic menu","Understand common Arab dishes and their cultural significance"],"canDoStatements":["I can order a meal in Arabic","I can tell a waiter my food preferences","I can recognize common Arabic dish names"],"prerequisites":["73a879d7-59c0-48d7-9006-9f46b7d4c3ba"],"estimatedMinutes":30},{"id":"011eafa1-a371-4b63-a133-c462b6ce2ec8","title":"Verb Patterns: Past Tense فَعَلَ","titleAr":"أوزان الأفعال: الماضي فَعَلَ","description":"Arabic verbs follow predictable patterns. The pattern فَعَلَ (fa'ala) is the foundation: كَتَبَ (he wrote), ذَهَبَ (he went), أَكَلَ (he ate). Learn to conjugate for أنا، أنتَ، هو، هي — and see how the root letters stay constant.","descriptionAr":"الأفعال العربية تتبع أنماطاً متوقعة. الوزن فَعَلَ هو الأساس: كتب، ذهب، أكل. تعلّم التصريف مع الضمائر","level":3,"orderIndex":1,"category":"grammar","skillFocus":"writing","imageUrl":null,"xpReward":90,"isPublished":true,"actflLevel":"Intermediate Mid","cefrLevel":"B1","objectives":["Conjugate past tense verbs for all pronouns","Recognize the فَعَلَ pattern as the base verb form","Use past tense in sentences and narration","Identify root letters within conjugated verbs"],"canDoStatements":["I can talk about what I did yesterday in Arabic","I can conjugate common verbs in past tense","I can tell a simple story about past events"],"prerequisites":["7014428a-55c4-4b90-9406-7b4433885789"],"estimatedMinutes":40},{"id":"138a29ce-9fe1-4900-ba82-3c06bbb9b133","title":"Present Tense: يَفْعَلُ Pattern","titleAr":"المضارع: وزن يَفْعَلُ","description":"Build on past tense knowledge. كَتَبَ (he wrote) → يَكْتُبُ (he writes). Learn the prefix system: أَكْتُبُ (I write), تَكْتُبُ (you write), نَكْتُبُ (we write). See how Arabic elegantly marks person, gender, and number in one word.","descriptionAr":"ابنِ على معرفتك بالماضي. كَتَبَ → يَكتُبُ. تعلّم نظام السوابق واللواحق","level":3,"orderIndex":2,"category":"grammar","skillFocus":"writing","imageUrl":null,"xpReward":100,"isPublished":true,"actflLevel":"Intermediate Mid","cefrLevel":"B1","objectives":["Conjugate present tense verbs with prefix system","Compare past and present tense patterns","Express habitual actions and current states","Use present tense in daily conversation"],"canDoStatements":["I can describe my daily routine in Arabic","I can say what I am doing right now","I can express habits and regular activities"],"prerequisites":["011eafa1-a371-4b63-a133-c462b6ce2ec8"],"estimatedMinutes":40},{"id":"fbe09321-9b13-4dc3-b083-3e917acfd145","title":"Question Words & Asking Questions","titleAr":"أدوات الاستفهام وطرح الأسئلة","description":"Ask anything in Arabic! Learn مَن (who), ماذا (what), أين (where), متى (when), لماذا (why), كيف (how), كم (how many). Practice with real-life questions: أين المطار؟ كم الساعة؟ ماذا تريد؟","descriptionAr":"اسأل أي سؤال بالعربية! تعلّم من، ماذا، أين، متى، لماذا، كيف، كم مع أسئلة واقعية","level":3,"orderIndex":3,"category":"grammar","skillFocus":"speaking","imageUrl":null,"xpReward":90,"isPublished":true,"actflLevel":"Intermediate Mid","cefrLevel":"B1","objectives":["Use 7 question words correctly in sentences","Form questions from statements","Ask practical real-life questions","Understand and respond to common questions"],"canDoStatements":["I can ask where, when, why, how questions in Arabic","I can ask for directions and information","I can understand common questions people ask me"],"prerequisites":["138a29ce-9fe1-4900-ba82-3c06bbb9b133"],"estimatedMinutes":30},{"id":"920e7e54-53dc-46fc-b541-c76141cffe49","title":"Describing People & Places","titleAr":"وصف الأشخاص والأماكن","description":"Adjectives follow nouns in Arabic and must agree in gender! بَيت كَبير (big house) vs مَدينة كَبيرة (big city). Learn 20 essential adjectives and the agreement rule that makes Arabic descriptions precise.","descriptionAr":"الصفات تتبع الأسماء وتتطابق في الجنس! بيت كبير مقابل مدينة كبيرة. تعلّم ٢٠ صفة أساسية","level":3,"orderIndex":4,"category":"vocabulary","skillFocus":"writing","imageUrl":null,"xpReward":90,"isPublished":true,"actflLevel":"Intermediate Mid","cefrLevel":"B1","objectives":["Use 20 essential Arabic adjectives","Apply noun-adjective gender agreement","Describe people, places and objects in detail","Use comparative forms (bigger, smaller)"],"canDoStatements":["I can describe a person's appearance in Arabic","I can describe a place with multiple adjectives","I can compare two things using Arabic adjectives"],"prerequisites":["fbe09321-9b13-4dc3-b083-3e917acfd145"],"estimatedMinutes":35}]
