4:03:08 PM [express] GET /api/lessons/c3151c6b-b3ba-43a3-b066-b0535adb5415 200 in 4ms :: {"id":"c3151c6b-b3ba-43a3-b066-b0535adb5415","title":"The Arabic Letter System","titleAr":"نظام الحروف العربية","description":"Discover how Arabic letters change shape based on their position in a word. Learn the 4 forms: isolated, initial, medial, and final — starting with Alif (أ), Ba (ب), Ta (ت), and Tha (ث).","descriptionAr":"اكتشف كيف تتغير أشكال الحروف العربية حسب موقعها في الكلمة. تعلّم الأشكال الأربعة: المنفرد، البداية، الوسط، والنهاية","level":1,"orderIndex":1,"category":"alphabet","skillFocus":"reading","imageUrl":null,"xpReward":60,"isPublished":true,"actflLevel":"Novice Low","cefrLevel":"A1","objectives":["Recognize all 28 Arabic letters in their isolated forms","Identify letter families by shared base shapes","Distinguish letters by their dot patterns","Write basic letter shapes with correct stroke direction","Pronounce each letter with its correct sound"],"canDoStatements":["I can recognize Arabic letters when I see them","I can name the 28 letters of the Arabic alphabet","I can write individual Arabic letters","I can pronounce each letter's basic sound"],"prerequisites":[],"estimatedMinutes":25}
4:03:08 PM [express] GET /api/lessons/c3151c6b-b3ba-43a3-b066-b0535adb5415/exercises 200 in 9ms :: [{"id":"0b969664-ba90-4f23-9196-e0efcc7dde99","lessonId":"c3151c6b-b3ba-43a3-b066-b0535adb5415","type":"multiple_choice","difficulty":1,"question":"Arabic letters change shape based on their position in a word. How many forms does each letter have?","questionAr":"الحروف العربية تتغير حسب موقعها في الكلمة. كم شكلاً لكل حرف؟","context":"Unlike English where 'a' always looks the same, Arabic letters like ب can look like بـ ـبـ ـب depending on where they appear in a word.","contextAr":"على عكس الإنجليزية، الحروف العربية مثل ب تتغير شكلها حسب موقعها في الكلمة","hint":"Think about it: isolated, start of word, middle of word, end of word","hintAr":null,"options":["2 forms","3 forms","4 forms","5 forms"],"correctAnswer":"4 forms","explanation":"Each Arabic letter has 4 forms: isolated (ب), initial (بـ), medial (ـبـ), and final (ـب). This is because Arabic is written in connected script.","explanationAr":"لكل حرف ٤ أشكال: منفرد (ب)، بداية (بـ)، وسط (ـبـ)، نهاية (ـب)","grammarNote":"Some letters like أ (Alif), د (Dal), ذ (Dhal), ر (Ra), ز (Zay), و (Waw) only connect from the right side, so they only have 2 distinct forms.","grammarNoteAr":"بعض الحروف مثل أ، د، ذ، ر، ز، و تتصل من اليمين فقط، لذا لها شكلان فقط","skillType":"reading","xpReward":10,"orderIndex":1},{"id":"d7010924-b932-4929-967d-abace36c111f","lessonId":"c3151c6b-b3ba-43a3-b066-b0535adb5415","type":"multiple_choice","difficulty":1,"question":"Which letter is this: ب","questionAr":"ما هذا الحرف: ب","context":"ب (Ba) is the second letter of the Arabic alphabet. It sounds like the English 'b' in 'book'.\n\nVocabulary: ب is for بَاب (baab) = door, بِنْت (bint) = girl, بَيْت (bayt) = house","contextAr":"ب (الباء) هي الحرف الثاني في الأبجدية العربية. تشبه 'b' في الإنجليزية.\n\nمفردات: ب = باب، بنت، بيت","hint":null,"hintAr":null,"options":["Ta (ت)","Ba (ب)","Tha (ث)","Alif (ا)"],"correctAnswer":"Ba (ب)","explanation":"This is ب (Ba). It has ONE dot below. Compare: ت (Ta) has TWO dots above, ث (Tha) has THREE dots above.","explanationAr":"هذا ب (الباء). لها نقطة واحدة تحتها. قارن: ت (نقطتان فوق)، ث (ثلاث نقاط فوق)","grammarNote":null,"grammarNoteAr":null,"skillType":"reading","xpReward":10,"orderIndex":2},{"id":"088aa20e-5879-4fc6-b596-57cce0d05e5f","lessonId":"c3151c6b-b3ba-43a3-b066-b0535adb5415","type":"multiple_choice","difficulty":1,"question":"The word بَاب means 'door'. What sound does the first letter ب make?","questionAr":"كلمة بَاب تعني 'door'. ما صوت الحرف الأول ب؟","context":"New vocabulary:\n• بَاب (baab) = door\n• بِنْت (bint) = girl\n• بَيْت (bayt) = house\n\nAll three words start with ب (Ba), which sounds like English 'b'.","contextAr":"مفردات جديدة:\n• بَاب = door\n• بِنْت = girl\n• بَيْت = house","hint":null,"hintAr":null,"options":["Like 'p' in 'pen'","Like 'b' in 'book'","Like 'f' in 'fun'","Like 'm' in 'map'"],"correctAnswer":"Like 'b' in 'book'","explanation":"ب (Ba) sounds like 'b' in 'book'. Remember: بَاب (door), بِنْت (girl), بَيْت (house) — all start with the 'b' sound.","explanationAr":"ب تنطق مثل 'b' في الإنجليزية. تذكر: باب، بنت، بيت — كلها تبدأ بصوت 'ب'","grammarNote":null,"grammarNoteAr":null,"skillType":"reading","xpReward":10,"orderIndex":3},{"id":"529e88b1-752f-4169-bcb7-e078181614c3","lessonId":"c3151c6b-b3ba-43a3-b066-b0535adb5415","type":"multiple_choice","difficulty":1,"question":"How many dots does ت (Ta) have, and where are they?","questionAr":"كم نقطة لـ ت (التاء)، وأين هي؟","context":"New vocabulary:\n• تَمْر (tamr) = dates (the fruit)\n• ثَلْج (thalj) = snow\n\nThe letters ب، ت، ث all have the same base shape — only the dots differ! This is the key to telling them apart.","contextAr":"مفردات جديدة:\n• تَمْر = dates\n• ثَلْج = snow\n\nالحروف ب، ت، ث لها نفس الشكل الأساسي — فقط النقاط تختلف!","hint":null,"hintAr":null,"options":["1 dot below","2 dots above","3 dots above","No dots"],"correctAnswer":"2 dots above","explanation":"ت (Ta) has 2 dots ABOVE. Remember the pattern: ب (1 dot below) → ت (2 dots above) → ث (3 dots above). Dots are the key!","explanationAr":"ت لها نقطتان فوق. تذكر: ب (نقطة تحت) → ت (نقطتان فوق) → ث (ثلاث نقاط فوق)","grammarNote":null,"grammarNoteAr":null,"skillType":"reading","xpReward":10,"orderIndex":4},{"id":"e80a65e0-9647-450f-8fc4-282ae8cb5263","lessonId":"c3151c6b-b3ba-43a3-b066-b0535adb5415","type":"multiple_choice","difficulty":1,"question":"Look at the word بِنْت (bint = girl). Which letters do you recognize?","questionAr":"انظر لكلمة بِنْت (girl). أي حروف تعرفها؟","context":"بِنْت (bint) = girl. This word uses:\n• ب (Ba) — 1 dot below\n• ن (Nun) — like a bowl with 1 dot above\n• ت (Ta) — 2 dots above\n\nYou already know ب and ت from this lesson!","contextAr":"بِنْت = girl. الكلمة تستخدم: ب (نقطة تحت)، ن (مثل وعاء مع نقطة فوق)، ت (نقطتان فوق)","hint":null,"hintAr":null,"options":["Only ب","Only ت","Both ب and ت","Neither ب nor ت"],"correctAnswer":"Both ب and ت","explanation":"بِنْت starts with ب (Ba) and ends with ت (Ta). You know both! The middle letter ن (Nun) sounds like 'n' in 'nun'.","explanationAr":"بِنْت تبدأ بـ ب وتنتهي بـ ت. تعرفهما! الحرف الأوسط ن (النون) ينطق مثل 'n'","grammarNote":null,"grammarNoteAr":null,"skillType":"reading","xpReward":10,"orderIndex":5},{"id":"1bd0e21a-1c97-470a-9db0-52858f7100b7","lessonId":"c3151c6b-b3ba-43a3-b066-b0535adb5415","type":"fill_blank","difficulty":1,"question":"ب has 1 dot, ت has 2 dots. How many dots does ث have? ___","questionAr":"ب لها نقطة واحدة، ت لها نقطتان. كم نقطة لـ ث؟ ___","context":"ث (Tha) sounds like 'th' in 'think'. It appears in: ثَلْج (thalj) = snow, ثَمَر (thamar) = fruit.\n\nPattern: ب (1) → ت (2) → ث (?)","contextAr":"ث (الثاء) تنطق مثل 'th' في 'think'. تظهر في: ثَلْج = snow، ثَمَر = fruit","hint":"Follow the pattern: 1, 2, ___","hintAr":"اتبع النمط: ١، ٢، ___","options":null,"correctAnswer":"3","explanation":"ث has 3 dots above. The pattern: ب (1 dot below), ت (2 dots above), ث (3 dots above). Same shape, different dots!","explanationAr":"ث لها ثلاث نقاط فوق. النمط: ب (١)، ت (٢)، ث (٣). نفس الشكل، نقاط مختلفة!","grammarNote":null,"grammarNoteAr":null,"skillType":"reading","xpReward":15,"orderIndex":6},{"id":"03f0f13a-29f3-44ee-9600-1102a86ee1f8","lessonId":"c3151c6b-b3ba-43a3-b066-b0535adb5415","type":"multiple_choice","difficulty":1,"question":"أ (Alif) is the first letter of the Arabic alphabet. Which English vowel sound does it represent?","questionAr":"أ (الألف) هو أول حرف في الأبجدية. أي صوت في الإنجليزية يمثل؟","context":"أ (Alif) makes an 'a' or 'ah' sound. It's special: Alif is one of the non-connecting letters — it only connects to the letter before it, not after.\n\nNew words with Alif:\n• أَب (ab) = father\n• أُم (umm) = mother","contextAr":"أ (الألف) ينطق 'آ'. هو حرف غير متصل — يتصل بما قبله فقط.\n\nكلمات بالألف:\n• أَب = father\n• أُم = mother","hint":null,"hintAr":null,"options":["Like 'b' in 'book'","Like 'a' in 'father'","Like 'th' in 'think'","Like 't' in 'top'"],"correctAnswer":"Like 'a' in 'father'","explanation":"أ (Alif) makes the 'a' sound as in 'father'. It's the first letter of the Arabic alphabet and one of the most important!","explanationAr":"أ (الألف) ينطق مثل 'آ'. هو أول حرف في الأبجدية وأحد أهم الحروف","grammarNote":null,"grammarNoteAr":null,"skillType":"reading","xpReward":10,"orderIndex":7},{"id":"f428ec4e-8c69-4d2f-8197-1ee5cd864a67","lessonId":"c3151c6b-b3ba-43a3-b066-b0535adb5415","type":"sentence_order","difficulty":1,"question":"Arrange these letters by number of dots: least dots first → most dots last","questionAr":"رتّب هذه الحروف حسب عدد النقاط: الأقل أولاً","context":"You learned: ب (1 dot below), ت (2 dots above), ث (3 dots above), أ (no dots).","contextAr":"تعلمت: أ (بلا نقاط)، ب (١ نقطة)، ت (٢ نقاط)، ث (٣ نقاط)","hint":null,"hintAr":null,"options":["ث (3 dots)","ب (1 dot)","أ (no dots)","ت (2 dots)"],"correctAnswer":"أ (no dots) ب (1 dot) ت (2 dots) ث (3 dots)","explanation":"أ (0 dots) → ب (1 dot below) → ت (2 dots above) → ث (3 dots above). The dot pattern is the key to telling these letters apart!","explanationAr":"أ (٠) → ب (١) → ت (٢) → ث (٣). نمط النقاط هو المفتاح للتمييز بين الحروف!","grammarNote":null,"grammarNoteAr":null,"skillType":"reading","xpReward":15,"orderIndex":8},{"id":"eabaa6dd-1589-460d-8f0d-1d700e3df079","lessonId":"c3151c6b-b3ba-43a3-b066-b0535adb5415","type":"multiple_choice","difficulty":1,"question":"When ب appears in the MIDDLE of a word (medial position), what does it look like?","questionAr":"عندما تظهر ب في وسط الكلمة (الموضع الأوسط)، كيف تبدو؟","context":"Arabic letters connect like cursive writing. ب changes shape in each position:\n• Isolated: ب\n• Initial (start): بـ\n• Medial (middle): ـبـ\n• Final (end): ـب","contextAr":"الحروف العربية تتصل كالكتابة المتصلة. ب تتغير في كل موضع:\n• منفرد: ب\n• بداية: بـ\n• وسط: ـبـ\n• نهاية: ـب","hint":null,"hintAr":null,"options":["ب","بـ","ـبـ","ـب"],"correctAnswer":"ـبـ","explanation":"ـبـ is the medial (middle) form of ب. Notice the connecting lines on both sides. In بيت (house), the ب is at the start (بـ) and connects to ي in the middle.","explanationAr":"ـبـ هي الشكل الأوسط لـ ب. لاحظ خطوط الاتصال من الجانبين","grammarNote":null,"grammarNoteAr":null,"skillType":"reading","xpReward":15,"orderIndex":9},{"id":"56a7f339-2b47-4885-9db3-25da638b1d27","lessonId":"c3151c6b-b3ba-43a3-b066-b0535adb5415","type":"free_writing","difficulty":1,"question":"Write the Arabic letter that sounds like 'b' in 'book' and has ONE dot below it.","questionAr":"اكتب الحرف العربي الذي ينطق مثل 'b' وله نقطة واحدة تحته","context":"You learned this letter in exercise 2. It's the second letter of the Arabic alphabet. It starts words like بَاب (door) and بِنْت (girl).","contextAr":"تعلمت هذا الحرف في التمرين الثاني. هو الحرف الثاني في الأبجدية. يبدأ كلمات مثل باب وبنت","hint":null,"hintAr":null,"options":null,"correctAnswer":"ب","explanation":"ب (Ba) — 1 dot below, sounds like 'b'. You now know 4 letters: أ، ب، ت، ث — the first 4 letters of the Arabic alphabet!","explanationAr":"ب (الباء) — نقطة واحدة تحت، ينطق 'ب'. تعرف الآن ٤ حروف: أ، ب، ت، ث","grammarNote":null,"grammarNoteAr":null,"skillType":"writing","xpReward":20,"orderIndex":10}]
4:03:26 PM [express] GET /api/practice/adaptive 200 in 15ms :: [{"id":"0474a766-e749-4084-81eb-242c0464f103","lessonId":"ddeeec6b-63bf-46cf-bc0a-15b266d084b1","type":"multiple_choice","difficulty":1,"question":"In Arabic, 'the' is always الـ (al-). But the pronunciation changes! In 'القمر' (al-qamar = the moon), you say 'al-qamar'. But in 'الشمس' (ash-shams = the sun), the 'l' disappears! Why?","questionAr":"في العربية، 'the' هي دائماً الـ. لكن النطق يتغير! في 'القمر' تقول 'al-qamar'. في 'الشمس' تقول 'ash-shams'. لماذا تختفي اللام؟","context":"New vocabulary:\n• الشَّمْس (ash-shams) = the sun\n• القَمَر (al-qamar) = the moon\n• الـ (al-) = the (definite article)\n\nArabic letters are divided into:\n• Moon Letters (حروف قمرية): الـ keeps its 'l' sound. القمر = al-qamar\n• Sun Letters (حروف شمسية): the 'l' assimilates into the next letter. الشمس = ash-shams (not al-shams)","contextAr":"مفردات جديدة:\n• الشَّمْس = the sun\n• القَمَر = the moon\n• الـ = 'the'\n\nالحروف تنقسم إلى: قمرية (الـ تبقى) وشمسية (الـ تستوعب في الحرف التالي)","hint":null,"hintAr":null,"options":["Arabic doesn't have 'l' sounds","The letter after الـ 'swallows' the L sound","الـ has no L in this context","The moon is special in Arabic"],"correctAnswer":"The letter after الـ 'swallows' the L sound","explanation":"Sun Letters assimilate the 'l'. الشمس = ash-SHAMS (not al-shams). The ش 'absorbs' the ل. This happens with 14 of the 28 Arabic letters.","explanationAr":"الحروف الشمسية تستوعب اللام. الشمس = اشـشَمس. الشين تستوعب اللام","grammarNote":null,"grammarNoteAr":null,"skillType":"reading","xpReward":10,"orderIndex":1},{"id":"6ada3b29-5eb7-47d2-9da0-7a11fa0815d5","lessonId":"fcc364c5-9911-4ee8-8a5d-5a4f8eb3a520","type":"multiple_choice","difficulty":1,"question":"شَدَّة (shadda) ّ is a special mark. What does it do?","questionAr":"الشَّدَّة ّ علامة خاصة. ماذا تفعل؟","context":"New vocabulary: شَدَّة (shadda) = doubling mark\n\nWhen you see ّ on a letter, that letter is DOUBLED (said twice but written once).\nExample: مُدَرِّس (mudarris) = teacher — رِّ has shadda = 'rr' sound","contextAr":"مفردات جديدة: شَدَّة = علامة التضعيف\n\nعندما ترى ّ على حرف، يُضاعَف ذلك الحرف (يُقال مرتين ويُكتب مرة).\nمثال: مُدَرِّس = teacher — رِّ مع شدة = صوت 'رر'","hint":null,"hintAr":null,"options":["Makes the letter silent","Doubles the letter","Adds an 'a' sound","Removes the letter"],"correctAnswer":"Doubles the letter","explanation":"شَدَّة (shadda) doubles the letter. مُدَرِّس (mudarris = teacher) — the رِّ is said as 'rr'. كلمة شَدَّة itself has shadda on the دّ!","explanationAr":"الشدة تضاعف الحرف. مُدَرِّس = teacher — الرِّ يُنطق 'رر'. كلمة شَدَّة نفسها مع شدة على الدّ!","grammarNote":null,"grammarNoteAr":null,"skillType":"reading","xpReward":10,"orderIndex":6},{"id":"cd737283-7122-4997-90b2-6707581c85cf","lessonId":"ddeeec6b-63bf-46cf-bc0a-15b266d084b1","type":"multiple_choice","difficulty":1,"question":"Quick check: Which of these is a Moon Letter (الـ keeps its 'l')?","questionAr":"اختبار سريع: أي من هذه حرف قمري (الـ تحتفظ باللام)؟","context":"Sun Letters (الـ assimilates): ت، ث، د، ذ، ر، ز، س، ش، ص، ض، ط، ظ، ل، ن\nMoon Letters (الـ keeps 'l'): أ، ب، ج، ح، خ، ع، غ، ف، ق، ك، م، ه، و، ي","contextAr":"الشمسية: ت، ث، د، ذ، ر، ز، س، ش، ص، ض، ط، ظ، ل، ن\nالقمرية: أ، ب، ج، ح، خ، ع، غ، ف، ق، ك، م، ه، و، ي","hint":null,"hintAr":null,"options":["ش (Shin)","ن (Nun)","م (Meem)","ت (Ta)"],"correctAnswer":"م (Meem)","explanation":"م (Meem) is a Moon Letter. الـ + word starting with م = al-m... (not am-m...). Examples: الماء (al-maa' = the water), المدرسة (al-madrasa = the school).","explanationAr":"م (الميم) حرف قمري. الـ + كلمة تبدأ بم = al-m... مثال: الماء، المدرسة","grammarNote":null,"grammarNoteAr":null,"skillType":"reading","xpReward":15,"orderIndex":8},{"id":"4b372af7-2468-4e2d-af50-8d0970bcdd88","lessonId":"ddeeec6b-63bf-46cf-bc0a-15b266d084b1","type":"multiple_choice","difficulty":1,"question":"الكِتَاب (al-kitaab = the book). كـ (Ka) is a Moon Letter. How do you pronounce الكتاب?","questionAr":"الكِتَاب = the book. كـ (Ka) حرف قمري. كيف تنطق الكتاب؟","context":"New vocabulary: الكِتَاب (al-kitaab) = the book\n\nYou know كِتَاب = book. Adding الـ: الكِتَاب = the book.\nSince ك is a Moon Letter, the الـ keeps its 'l': al-kitaab (not ak-kitaab).","contextAr":"مفردات جديدة: الكِتَاب = the book\n\nتعرف كِتَاب = book. بإضافة الـ: الكِتَاب = the book. ك حرف قمري، فالـ تبقى: al-kitaab","hint":null,"hintAr":null,"options":["ak-kitaab","al-kitaab","ash-kitaab","it-kitaab"],"correctAnswer":"al-kitaab","explanation":"الكِتَاب = al-kitaab. ك is a Moon Letter, so the الـ keeps its 'l' sound. Moon Letters: أ، ب، ج، ح، خ، ع، غ، ف، ق، ك، م، ه، و، ي","explanationAr":"الكِتَاب = al-kitaab. ك حرف قمري، فالـ تحتفظ بالـلام. الحروف القمرية: أ، ب، ج، ح، خ، ع، غ، ف، ق، ك، م، ه، و، ي","grammarNote":null,"grammarNoteAr":null,"skillType":"reading","xpReward":10,"orderIndex":2},{"id":"384df65d-3422-4f73-8c9e-785f5e09d1f4","lessonId":"d9a0d0af-1c1a-4552-b0a0-91d4bcd2bd20","type":"multiple_choice","difficulty":1,"question":"The most universal Arabic greeting is السَّلامُ عَلَيْكُم (as-salaamu alaykum). What does it literally mean?","questionAr":"التحية العربية الأشمل هي السَّلامُ عَلَيْكُم. ما معناها الحرفي؟","context":"New vocabulary:\n• السَّلامُ (as-salaamu) = the peace (from root س-ل-م)\n• عَلَيْكُم ('alaykum) = upon you (plural)\n• So: السلام عليكم = 'Peace be upon you'\n\nThis greeting is used by all Arabic speakers, Muslim and non-Muslim. It's always appropriate!","contextAr":"مفردات جديدة:\n• السَّلامُ = السلام (من س-ل-م)\n• عَلَيْكُم = عليكم (جمع)\n• السلام عليكم = 'Peace be upon you'\n\nهذه التحية تستخدمها كل الناطقين بالعربية","hint":null,"hintAr":null,"options":["Good morning","Hello, how are you?","Peace be upon you","Welcome to my home"],"correctAnswer":"Peace be upon you","explanation":"السلام عليكم = 'Peace be upon you'. From root س-ل-م (peace/safety), which also gives us: سَلِيم (healthy), إسلام (submission to God), مُسلم (Muslim).","explanationAr":"السلام عليكم = 'Peace be upon you'. من الجذر س-ل-م الذي يعطينا: سَلِيم، إسلام، مُسلم","grammarNote":null,"grammarNoteAr":null,"skillType":"speaking","xpReward":10,"orderIndex":1},{"id":"1bd0e21a-1c97-470a-9db0-52858f7100b7","lessonId":"c3151c6b-b3ba-43a3-b066-b0535adb5415","type":"fill_blank","difficulty":1,"question":"ب has 1 dot, ت has 2 dots. How many dots does ث have? ___","questionAr":"ب لها نقطة واحدة، ت لها نقطتان. كم نقطة لـ ث؟ ___","context":"ث (Tha) sounds like 'th' in 'think'. It appears in: ثَلْج (thalj) = snow, ثَمَر (thamar) = fruit.\n\nPattern: ب (1) → ت (2) → ث (?)","contextAr":"ث (الثاء) تنطق مثل 'th' في 'think'. تظهر في: ثَلْج = snow، ثَمَر = fruit","hint":"Follow the pattern: 1, 2, ___","hintAr":"اتبع النمط: ١، ٢، ___","options":null,"correctAnswer":"3","explanation":"ث has 3 dots above. The pattern: ب (1 dot below), ت (2 dots above), ث (3 dots above). Same shape, different dots!","explanationAr":"ث لها ثلاث نقاط فوق. النمط: ب (١)، ت (٢)، ث (٣). نفس الشكل، نقاط مختلفة!","grammarNote":null,"grammarNoteAr":null,"skillType":"reading","xpReward":15,"orderIndex":6},{"id":"65dfbb70-13ec-442e-a615-5e723678e682","lessonId":"d6f23458-f5c9-47fe-adce-7e309aec5ba4","type":"sentence_order","difficulty":1,"question":"Match: Put each word next to its meaning","questionAr":"طابق: ضع كل كلمة بجانب معناها","context":"You learned 5 words this lesson. Let's review them all.","contextAr":"تعلمت ٥ كلمات في هذا الدرس. لنراجعها جميعاً","hint":null,"hintAr":null,"options":["بَاب","بَيْت","بِنْت"],"correctAnswer":"بَيْت بِنْت بَاب","explanation":"Order: بَيْت (house) → بِنْت (girl) → بَاب (door). All three start with ب!","explanationAr":"الترتيب: بَيْت (house) → بِنْت (girl) → بَاب (door). كلها تبدأ بـ ب!","grammarNote":null,"grammarNoteAr":null,"skillType":"reading","xpReward":15,"orderIndex":8},{"id":"13de6099-4c50-420c-812f-acb533c48a2d","lessonId":"d6f23458-f5c9-47fe-adce-7e309aec5ba4","type":"multiple_choice","difficulty":1,"question":"The word تَمْر (tamr) starts with ت. What does تَمْر mean?","questionAr":"كلمة تَمْر تبدأ بـ ت. ماذا تعني تَمْر؟","context":"New vocabulary:\n• تَمْر (tamr) = dates (the sweet fruit from palm trees)\n• تَمْر is very important in Arab culture — it's the first food offered to guests!\n\nتَمْر starts with ت (Ta) which you learned in Lesson 1.","contextAr":"مفردات جديدة:\n• تَمْر = dates (الفاكهة من النخيل)\n• التمر مهم جداً في الثقافة العربية — أول طعام يُقدَّم للضيوف!","hint":null,"hintAr":null,"options":["Sugar","Bread","Dates (fruit)","Water"],"correctAnswer":"Dates (fruit)","explanation":"تَمْر (tamr) = dates. This sweet fruit from palm trees is a staple of Arab hospitality. تَمْر starts with ت (Ta, 2 dots above).","explanationAr":"تَمْر = dates. هذه الفاكهة من النخيل أساس الضيافة العربية. تبدأ بـ ت (نقطتان فوق)","grammarNote":null,"grammarNoteAr":null,"skillType":"reading","xpReward":10,"orderIndex":4}]
